    "created_at": "2018-02-16T14:15:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-16T14:16:24Z",
    "body": "I don't really understand what Chrome did here. In part this seems related to some new non-standardized code around cross-origin resources.\r\n\r\nFrom reading https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/content/common/cross_site_document_classifier.cc?rcl=55f740be72bda75edfe6ec4ef3963ba789c8abf5&l=84 it seems some parts of Chrome understand all these things to be JSON now:\r\n\r\n* text/x-json[+_whatever_]\r\n* text/json[+_whatever_]\r\n* application/json[+_whatever_]\r\n* [_whatever_]+json\r\n\r\nAnd these as XML:\r\n\r\n* text/xml[+_whatever_]\r\n* application/xml[+_whatever_]\r\n* [_whatever_]+xml\r\n\r\nHowever, judging from how that code is used it may or may not affect `XMLHttpRequest`, page loading, and other pieces using the XML MIME type definition. I don't think much uses the JSON MIME type definition currently, but the same concern applies there.\r\n\r\ncc @domenic ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
