    "updated_at": "2018-02-16T16:39:22Z",
    "body": "Right, this is all done in preparation for some upcoming standardization work; this issue was filed while noticing a mismatch.\r\n\r\nThe XML MIME types mismatch is interesting and perhaps another bug.\r\n\r\nRight now the spec only uses \"JSON MIME type\" to determine whether to display something as a text file or not. This is somewhat testable, although the spec has an escape hatch where there can be \"explicitly supported JSON types\" that don't get treated as plain text.\r\n\r\nSo I think we should be open to changing the definition of JSON MIME type if a better use (like the cross-origin resource blocking) comes along. In the meantime we can just use this as a tracking issue.",
